{"title":"Career Roadmap · Utilities Planning Engineer","role":"Utilities Planning Engineer","summary":"A Utilities Planning Engineer plans, coordinates, analyzes, and optimizes urban and infrastructure utility networks such as:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Smart Infrastructure / Smart Cities Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Utilities Planning Engineer plans, coordinates, analyzes, and optimizes urban and infrastructure utility networks such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water supply"},{"text":"Sewerage"},{"text":"Stormwater drainage"},{"text":"Electricity distribution"},{"text":"Gas networks"},{"text":"District cooling/heating"},{"text":"Telecommunications"},{"text":"Solid-waste infrastructure"},{"text":"Smart utility systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a Smart Infrastructure / Smart Cities graduate, the strongest career profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Infrastructure Engineering","GIS","Utility Network Planning","CAD/BIM","Hydraulic/Electrical Analysis","Data Analytics","Smart City Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits between engineering design, urban planning, GIS, asset management, and infrastructure project delivery."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E. Smart Infrastructure","Engineering Fundamentals","Surveying + GIS + CAD","Urban Infrastructure Systems","Water + Sewerage + Stormwater","Power + Telecom + Gas Utility Basics","Utility Network Mapping","Hydraulic / Network Analysis","Demand Forecasting","Utility Corridor Planning","BIM + GIS + Digital Infrastructure","Smart Utility Analytics","Infrastructure Internship","Utility Planning Engineer","Senior Utility Planning Engineer","Utility Planning Lead / Infrastructure Manager","Smart Infrastructure / Digital Utilities Lead"]}]},