":"Utility-network/GIS platforms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3 — Water & Environmental Utilities"},{"type":"p","text":"A Utilities Planning Engineer should have a strong understanding of water-related infrastructure."},{"type":"h","text":"Water Supply"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water demand"},{"text":"Population projections"},{"text":"Per-capita demand"},{"text":"Peak demand"},{"text":"Water distribution networks"},{"text":"Storage reservoirs"},{"text":"Pumping stations"},{"text":"Transmission pipelines"},{"text":"Distribution pipelines"},{"text":"Pressure management"},{"text":"Leakage"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Network Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Flow"},{"text":"Pressure"},{"text":"Head loss"},{"text":"Pipe diameter"},{"text":"Pump characteristics"},{"text":"Network balancing"},{"text":"Hydraulic constraints"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools worth learning include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EPANET"},{"text":"WaterGEMS or equivalent hydraulic modelling software"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sewerage Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sewage generation"},{"text":"Sewer network planning"},{"text":"Gravity flow"},{"text":"Pumping systems"},{"text":"Sewer profiles"},{"text":"Manholes"},{"text":"Treatment infrastructure"},{"text":"Infiltration/inflow"},{"text":"Capacity assessment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Peak flow"},{"text":"Pipe slope"},{"text":"Velocity"},{"text":"Hydraulic capacity"},{"text":"Overflow risks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stormwater Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Catchment delineation"},{"text":"Rainfall analysis"},{"text":"Runoff estimation"},{"text":"Drainage networks"},{"text":"Stormwater channels"},{"text":"Culverts"},{"text":"Detention/retention systems"},{"text":"Flood-prone areas"},{"text":"Sustainable drainage"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful concepts:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rational method"},{"text":"IDF curves"},{"text":"Hydrographs"},{"text":"Watersheds"},{"text":"Flood modelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Multi-Utility Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"The major difference between a conventional civil engineer and a strong utilities planner is the ability to understand multiple utility systems together."},{"type":"h","text":"Electricity"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Distribution networks"},{"text":"Feeders"},{"text":"Transformers"},{"text":"Substations"},{"text":"Load demand"},{"text":"Peak load"},{"text":"Power quality"},{"text":"Underground cabling"},{"text":"Utility corridors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to become a protection engineer, but you should understand enough electrical distribution engineering to coordinate utility planning."},{"type":"h","text":"Telecommunications"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fiber-optic networks"},{"text":"Duct banks"},{"text":"Telecom corridors"},{"text":"Underground cable routes"},{"text":"Network nodes"},{"text":"Broadband infrastructure"},{"text":"5G small-cell infrastructure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Gas Utilities"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pipeline networks"},{"text":"Pressure levels"},{"text":"Regulators"},{"text":"Distribution systems"},{"text":"Safety zones"},{"text":"Utility corridors"},{"text":"Pipeline integrity basics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Gas infrastructure involves significant safety and regulatory requirements, so project-specific codes and local regulations must always be followed."},{"type":"h","text":"District Energy"},{"type":"p","text":"For modern smart cities, understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"District cooling"},{"text":"District heating"},{"text":"Centralized energy systems"},{"text":"Chilled-water networks"},{"text":"Thermal storage"},{"text":"Energy distribution"},{"text":"Heat recovery"}]}